Subject: [PATCH] drm/bridge: lt9611: release the DT510 active-low reset

DT510 connects GPIO2_IO11 to the plain LT9611 RSTn input and correctly
describes the line as GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW. The legacy reset sequence uses
logical 1, 0, 1, leaving this active-low line physically low and the chip
held in reset before the driver reads its revision.

Use logical 0, 1, 0 to preserve the intended physical high, low, high
sequence and its 20/20/100 ms delays. Keep GPIOD_OUT_HIGH at acquisition:
logical 1 initially asserts the active-low reset while power is enabled.

Apply this patch only through the imx8mm-jaguar-dt510 SRC_URI override.
Other machine builds retain their legacy reset convention; do not apply
this unconditionally to boards using GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH in their DT.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [DT510-only adaptation of legacy GPIO semantics]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -532,13 +532,13 @@
 
 static void lt9611_reset(struct lt9611 *lt9611)
 {
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 1);
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 0);
 	msleep(20);
 
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 0);
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 1);
 	msleep(20);
 
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 1);
+	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(lt9611->reset_gpio, 0);
 	msleep(100);
 }
 
